                    {
                        "sense_id": "bb2d6fd4-7a9e-3e00-9ca1-4a94b5c7f671",
                        "entry_id": "80e4d10c-e529-3cde-bcc8-ab3a1ce62c6e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of condemnatory."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fcee2ca3-8d32-4b6e-88c6-08b77ce6430f",
                                "sense_id": "bb2d6fd4-7a9e-3e00-9ca1-4a94b5c7f671",
                                "text": "Of course, the mites of sympathy, of friendly feelings towards Denmark which are mingled with your condemning judgments, are withheld by the German papers; but, seriously speaking, I cannot see that they do anything but render your concluding sentences the more condemning."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e042038-7d1f-4c7c-a68b-6dc22654ef4f",
                                "sense_id": "bb2d6fd4-7a9e-3e00-9ca1-4a94b5c7f671",
                                "text": "Ah, my Brethren, that is a very condemning thing, to sin against a tender conscience."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd25e8f5-e7bf-40d1-bdf4-68a0ab925891",
                                "sense_id": "bb2d6fd4-7a9e-3e00-9ca1-4a94b5c7f671",
                                "text": "Ironic remarks were considered more condemning than literal remarks, and direct remarks were considered more condemning than indirect ones, but these effects were independent and did not influence one another."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
